+## Classic raid augments · deployed for player testing
+
+Sixteen individually LORE trophies (963200–963215) use the existing type-22 chest socket. Each eligible boss corpse has one independent roll. Dragons have a 25% chance, secondary bosses 15% and planar finals 50%. Managed drops require credited Raid objectives. Capstones share a hard 90-second minimum including across swaps, zoning and relogging. The native second-resolution timer uses 91 ticks. The ordinary stock Deepwater Pearl 33961 and Phinigel’s augment 963202 share a display name. Yael’s public spawn still needs confirmation.
+
+The classic-raid-augments context points to E:/EQ_Local_Dev/_worktrees/classic-raid-augments-production. Main PR435/25219aac, test PR433/9e72a3ce. OVH stage classic-raid-augments-20261112-v2 uses full matched world/zone/shared_memory on the retained Inventory b737e641 source, preserving signed client 2026111202. The staged SQL passed replay and all 310,000 existing cache records were byte-identical alongside 16 new effective LORE records. See docs/releases/classic-raid-augments-20261112/deployed.json, native.json, QA.md, the wiki receipt and the 1,278-fight balance study. Separate the closed-then-reopened runtime verification from RoF2 player acceptance, still open.
